    {
      "@id": "README.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "(footer)",
      "prov:value": "*`README.md` and [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) are declared assets of this instance ([`cat-harness.json`](cat-harness.json), roles `instance-readme` and `agent-instructions`). Until 2026-09-20 this instance declared the **repository's** two files as its own, so the file a reader opened first answered \"what is this repository\" and \"what is this layer\" at once, and `check:subgraph-coverage` reported nothing because the asset did resolve — to the wrong file's job. Issue #592.*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "#592"
      ],
